!CHECK 221542.00 | 000000.40 8B 221614.74 02 | line 1 BB,SOWNER($11),JITSMC -IF MCP UNIT -- BB's first operand is a 24-bit bit address, so SOWNER's landed 0.32 is read TO THE BIT (0o40); the branch half carries J ITS MC, THIS page's line 48 at 221614.40, so 0o40 OR the BB code 0o34 = 0o74; byte 8B's low nibble is the $11 index
!CHECK 221543.00 | 000010.44 3C | line 2 LV,$2,SCREEL($12) -- 0o44 is 0o40 (bit 32 of SCREEL's landed 8.32) OR 2J = 4 for J=2; byte 3C's low nibble is the $12 index
!CHECK 221543.40 | 000000.42 82 036600.06 70 | line 3 LF(BU,30,6),.34($2) -PICK UP REEL NAME -- ".34" is a BARE DECIMAL bit offset, 34 bits = 0o42, which is the decimal-to-octal conversion checked outright; the second half word's 036600 carries length 0o36 = 30 and byte size 6, which is what settles the "3C" glyph in the statement field
!CHECK 221544.40 | 221600.34 C2 | line 4 BRZ,JITSSC -IF SCRATCH -- J ITS SC is THIS page's line 26 at 221600.00, so this is a real label check; the byte is C2 and not 02 (printed p.192 line 36 measured BRZ indexed by $1 as C3)
!CHECK 221545.00 | 221566.40 80 050000.12 F0 | line 5 SF(BU,40),JSPRNO -REEL NO. -- a VFL OPERAND, so J SPRNO's bit address is read TO THE BIT: 221566.40 is exactly what line 24 prints, which is the independent check on lines 22 and 23's character counts; 0o050000 is length 0o50 = 40
!CHECK 221546.00 | 221557.03 01 | line 6 LVI,$1,JLBMES -- J LBMES is THIS page's line 22 at 221557.00; .03 is 2J+1 for J=1 with bit 32 clear, so this pins the label's half word
!CHECK 221546.40 | 000000.32 8A 001000.00 F0 | line 7 J GETOF CM0000(BU,1),S CH OP($10) -- SCHOP's landed 0.26 gives 0o32; 001000.00 is the CM0000 comparand (CM1111 would print 001000.36, which is how the four round glyphs of "CMOCOO" are settled); byte 8A's low nibble is the $10 index.  printed p.135 line 41 prints this word for this statement
!CHECK 221547.40 | 215571.00 80 | line 8 SIC,SPRIMR -PUT REEL NO. IN MESSAGE -- a SIC reads EVERY BIT, so this row CHECKS SPRIMR's landed 215571.00
!CHECK 221550.00 | 215570.10 00 | line 9 B,SPRIME -OUT ON SPOOL -- a plain B shows bit 32 only; 0o10 is the B code and 00 the byte
!CHECK 221550.40 | 000103.40 80 | line 10 ,DSPR -- a NULL OPERATION, printed with an empty operation field; D SPR's landed 67.32 is word 0o103 bit 0o40
!CHECK 221551.00 | 000000.00 81 | line 11 ,0($1) -- null operation; byte 81's low nibble is the $1 index
!CHECK 221551.40 | 000001.00 80 | line 12 ,1.0 -- null operation
!CHECK 221552.00 | 215001.04 80 221554.74 02 | line 13 BB,SL,JPREOJ -- location carries a second asterisk.  BB's first operand is a 24-bit bit address so SL is read TO THE BIT at 215001.04, which CHECKS the landed value; the branch half carries J PREOJ, THIS page's line 17 at 221554.40 (0o40 OR 0o34 = 0o74)
!CHECK 221553.00 | 000405.35 01 | line 14 LVI,$14,SLABNG -IF AT PP LEVEL -- S LABNG's landed (16)105 = 0o405; .35 is 2J+1 = 29 for J=14 with bit 32 clear
!CHECK 221553.40 | 217451.40 80 | line 15 SIC,SDISIC -USE ERROR CONTROL -- a SIC, so this CHECKS SDISIC's landed 217451.40 to the bit
!CHECK 221554.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 16 B,SDISP -- half word only
!CHECK 221554.40 | 215571.00 80 | line 17 J PREOJ SIC,SPRIMR -IF AT MCP LEVEL -- the same word line 8 prints, from a second card; two identical words from two cards is the page's own check on the byte
!CHECK 221555.00 | 215570.10 00 | line 18 B,SPRIME -USE ABEOJ -- the same card as line 9
!CHECK 221555.40 | 000104.00 80 | line 19 ,DABEOJ -- null operation; D ABEOJ's landed (8)104.0.  printed p.132 line 44 prints the same word for the same card
!CHECK 221556.00 | 216242.10 00 | line 20 B,KSUPP -RETURN TO I/A IN MCP
!CHECK 221556.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 21 CNOP -- the counter stands at 221556.40, which is not a word boundary, so CNOP emits ONE NOP and the next card starts at 221557.00.  That is why line 21 prints a word at all and lines 35/36 (explicit NOPs) print the same one
!CHECK 221600.00 | 221350.00 80 | line 26 J ITSSC SIC,KCONVR -COMPUTE CH-UNIT NO. -- a SIC, so this CHECKS K CONVR's landed 221350.00; its LOCATION also closes the four DD cards' character counts
!CHECK 221600.40 | 221335.10 00 | line 27 B,KCONV
!CHECK 221601.00 | 221674.50+ | line 28 VF,JREPCU -- a VALUE FIELD is a 24-bit plus sign quantity (C22-6531 printed p.18), so the WHOLE bit address is deposited and this row reads J REP CU to the bit: 221674.50.  The sign prints as a trailing "+"
!CHECK 221601.40 | 221671.05 01 | line 29 LVI,$2,JREPSC -SET UP SCRATCH MESSAGE -- location carries a second asterisk.  .05 is 2J+1 for J=2 with bit 32 CLEAR, so this pins J REP SC to the first half word of 221671 and NOT to a bit; the .0 in the SYN above is a convention
!CHECK 221602.00 | 221721.00 10 | line 30 J TAKF LX,$0,JUNLDK -UNLOAD COMMAND -- 2J = 0 for J=0 and bit 32 is clear, so this pins J UNL DK's half word only
!CHECK 221602.40 | 221512.40 80 | line 31 SIC,KKRET -- a SIC, so this CHECKS K K RET's landed 221512.40
!CHECK 221603.00 | 221505.10 00 | line 32 B,KIOREJ
!CHECK 221603.40 | 221604.43 01 | line 33 LVI,$1,$+1.0 -WAIT FOR TERMINATION -- "$" is this row's own 221603.40, so $+1.0 is 221604.40: 0o40 OR 2J+1 = 0o03 for J=1 gives 0o43.  A real arithmetic check, not a symbol lookup
!CHECK 221604.00 | 221525.10 00 | line 34 B,JSEOPT -- J SEOP T is printed p.192's line 27 at 221525.00
!CHECK 221604.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 35 NOP
!CHECK 221605.00 | 000000.30 00 | line 36 NOP
!CHECK 221605.40 | 221602.10 00 | line 37 B,JTAKF -- J TAKF is THIS page's line 30 at 221602.00
!CHECK 221606.00 | 233666.04 80 001000.06 70 | line 38 LF(BU,1),JIOBSY -- a VFL OPERAND, so J IOBSY's landed 233666.04 is CHECKED to the bit; 001000 is length 1 and the byte 70 is LF, matching line 3's second half word byte for byte
!CHECK 221607.00 | 233666.00 80 001000.12 F0 | line 39 SF(BU,1),JWAIT -- a VFL operand, so J WAIT's landed 233666.00 is CHECKED to the bit; byte F0 is SF, matching line 5
!CHECK 221610.00 | 215470.40 80 | line 40 SIC,SCOMIC -TELL OPERATOR WHAT TO DO -- a SIC, so this CHECKS S COMIC's landed 215470.40
!CHECK 221610.40 | 215470.10 00 | line 41 B,SCOMM -- S COMM is 215470.00, one half word below S COMIC, and the pair is landed that way by printed p.116
!CHECK 221611.00 | 000000.00 82 | line 42 ,0.0($2) -- null operation; byte 82's low nibble is the $2 index
!CHECK 221611.40 | 000010.00 80 | line 43 ,8.0 -- null operation; 8 decimal is 0o10, another decimal-to-octal check
!CHECK 221612.00 | 221325.40 80 | line 44 SIC,KUNRR -- a SIC, so this CHECKS K UNRR's landed 221325.40.  Card serial LG000258
!CHECK 221612.40 | 221321.50 00 | line 45 B,KKLOOP -- K K LOOP's landed 221321.40: 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50, so the half word is checked.  Card serial LG000258 A SECOND TIME
!CHECK 221613.00 | 221617.00 80 000021.06 A0 | line 46 TI,3,JNEWXR,$1 -- the MIRROR of printed p.192's line 51 "TI,3,$1,JNEWXR", which prints 000021.00 80 221617.06 A0: the same two half words with the operands swapped.  "$1" is index register 1, whose cell is word 0o21.  The byte is A0 and not AC: I2 = 0 because the second operand carries no parenthesised index, and p.192 re-read its mirror at 1200 dpi for exactly this reason
!CHECK 221614.00 | 221614.10 00 | line 47 J NEWT B,$ -- "$" is this row's own 221614.00, so the row is self-referential and checks the location directly.  printed p.189 line 2 SICs J NEWT at (8)221614.0, which is what makes this page's origin CHECKED rather than asserted
!CHECK 221614.40 | 221350.00 80 | line 48 J ITSMC SIC,KCONVR -- the same card as line 26; line 1's branch half carries this label, so the two rows check each other
!CHECK 221615.00 | 221335.10 00 | line 49 B,KCONV -- the same statement as line 27, and THIS one carries the second asterisk while line 27 does not, which is one more counterexample to any statement-shaped rule for the mark
!CHECK 221615.40 | 221714.50+ | line 50 VF,JRCTCU -- a value field, so J RCT CU is read to the bit at 221714.50
!CHECK 221616.00 | 221711.05 01 | line 51 LVI,$2,JREPCT -- .05 is 2J+1 for J=2 with bit 32 clear, so J REP CT is pinned to the first half word of 221711 and the offset is NOT observed
!CHECK 221616.40 | 221602.10 00 | line 52 B,JTAKF -- the same card as line 37; the counter leaves this page at 221617.00
!
! >>> THE FOUR (A*)DD ROWS (22-25) PRINT NO BINARY, SO NO !CHECK
! >>> CAN NAME A WORD FOR THEM -- AND !SYM/!CHECK REACH ONLY THREE
! >>> OF THEIR FOUR BOUNDARIES. <<<  What is checked by the file
! above is:
!
!   !SYM JLBMES 221557.00   closes lines 1-21 (and CNOP)
!   !SYM JSPRNO 221566.40   closes lines 22+23 TOGETHER (38+22=60)
!   !CHECK 221600.00        closes lines 24+25 TOGETHER (36+40=76)
!   !CHECK 221545.00        line 5's SF reads J SPRNO BIT-EXACTLY,
!                           an independent reading of the same
!                           boundary
!
! The SPLIT inside each pair -- 38 against 22, and 36 against 40 --
! is pinned by the PRINTED LOCATIONS of lines 23 and 25, and those
! two rows carry no label and no binary, so the !CHECK/!SYM
! vocabulary cannot express them.  THEY WERE MEASURED ANYWAY, by
! assembling this deck with a synthetic label on each of those two
! cards (a scratchpad experiment; no label was added to the deck):
!
!   line 23 lands at 221563.60   page prints 221563.60
!   line 25 lands at 221573.00   page prints 221573.00
!   after line 52 the counter is 221617.00
!
! This probe is a CONSISTENCY check, not an independent witness --
! the assembler is counting the characters this deck types, so it
! cannot disagree about how many were typed.  What it establishes is
! that those counts reproduce the two printed locations exactly.
! See WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE item (c2) for what that does and does
! not buy, and THE COUNTER CHAIN for the independent leg.
